In `service.mjs`, the current implementation calls `validate(value)` and then assigns `store.value = value`. For the supplied input `'x'`, the source therefore predicts that the string is persisted. The coverage defect is that an implementation which omitted the assignment would still pass the supplied test.

A reproducible witness is to temporarily replace `save` with the following implementation and run `node existing.test.mjs`:

```js
export const save = (store, value, validate) => {
  validate(value);
};
